// Title: Windows AMSI Related Registry Tampering Via CommandLine
// ID: 7dbbcac2-57a0-45ac-b306-ff30a8bd2981
// Status: experimental
// Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-12-25
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
// Description: Detects tampering of AMSI (Anti-Malware Scan Interface) related registry values via command line tools such as reg.exe or PowerShell.
// AMSI provides a generic interface for applications and services to integrate with antimalware products.
// Adversaries may disable AMSI to evade detection of malicious scripts and code execution.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows Script\\Settings" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "AmsiEnable")) AND ((((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "Set-ItemProperty" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "New-ItemProperty" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "sp ")) AND (((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\powershell.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\pwsh.exe")) OR ((OriginalFileName = "PowerShell.EXE" OR OriginalFileName = "pwsh.dll")))) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "add") AND ((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\reg.exe") OR (OriginalFileName = "reg.exe")))))
